\title{karma2d: Two-Dimensional Kumaraswamy Autoregressive Moving Average Models}
\description{
Conditional maximum likelihood estimation, simulation, prediction and residual-based anomaly detection for the two-dimensional Kumaraswamy autoregressive moving average (2-D KARMA) model for bounded image data, in which each pixel follows a Kumaraswamy distribution in the median parametrization and the median follows a spatial ARMA structure over a strongly causal neighbourhood. Provides the Kumaraswamy distribution in the median parametrization, the analytic score vector, the conditional expected and observed information, quantile residuals, control-chart anomaly detection with morphological post-processing, and image quality metrics.
}
